
In vm_horizon mode, when the sky is cloudy and there are rocks or trees in the view, something that was added to improve performance actually worsened it; the frame rate is acceptable (not great but acceptable) until panning or walking, at which point the frame rate drops dismally low, to less than 1 fps.

In system view, if a planet is drawn near the host star and it has several moons, any attempt to click on the first 1 or 2 moons sometimes impinges on the host star's rectangle and selects the star instead. The hover+selection rectangle is a design choice for performance reasons, so in system view the moons' rectangles should get priority over the planets, which should get priority over the stars.

On sufficiently small moons and planets, rocks located past the horizon are visible through solid ground when they should be hidden.

